  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile avgpool is currently the strongest direction, with scvi_n200 reaching 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1 and outperforming pca_n2000 multiprofile avgpool (0.591 / 0.573) and single-profile PCA (0.485 / 0.464); avgpool also beat transformer for PCA. The key uncertainty is whether scvi_n200 is specifically better or whether another learned RNA encoder can match it under the same favorable profile and aggregation. config_008 tests scgpt with multiprofile avgpool, changing only the RNA encoder from the current best. This is a clean, high-information exploitation of the promising RNA-only pipeline, helps decide the best representation before adding image/fusion, and avoids prematurely testing multimodal configurations while image-only evidence remains weak."
}

